[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:declare-batch-fit-for-sale :finalize-food-safety-clearance :finalize-batch-clearance-decision :finalize-allergen-labeling-determination :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007211-cloud-itonami-isco-7211-metal-moulders-coremakers-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["declare the batch fit for sale" "declare this batch fit for sale" "finalize the food-safety clearance" "finalize the food safety clearance" "finalize the batch clearance decision" "finalize the allergen-labeling determination" "finalize the allergen labeling determination" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the shop safety officer judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799007512, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}", :actor/domain :food-processing/bakery-scheduling-logistics-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:baker-verified :bakery-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7512", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007512: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7512 Bakers, Pastry-cooks and Confectionery Makers bakery scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7512\n-- Bakers, Pastry-cooks and Confectionery Makers** only, Wave3\n(production/trades) of the rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3\nbatches 1-7 already landed: ~42 occupations so far).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7512\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"7512\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/technology`\nsibling present at the correct `../technology` relative path), and its\n`:name` read exactly \"Bakers, Pastry-cooks and Confectionery Makers\"\n-- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7512` (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7512` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nBakers, pastry-cooks and confectionery makers operate high-temperature\novens and handle food ingredients (some allergenic) -- real\nphysical-safety stakes (burn exposure) combined with a food-safety/\nallergen-labeling compliance dimension. The controlling constraint for\nthis vertical is that the closed op allowlist must NEVER include any\nop that directly finalizes a food-safety-clearance decision (e.g.\ndeclaring a batch fit for sale, an allergen-labeling determination),\nor overrides a shop safety officer's judgment -- those decisions must\nalways be a hard permanent block or an always-escalate op, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to BAKERY\nSCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs baking or\npreparation work, and never makes food-safety-clearance or\nallergen-labeling decisions itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211)\n(Metal Moulders and Coremakers: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor`\nsplit, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same wave, closest\nhot-process/heat-exposure workshop-safety domain shape) -- cloned and\nread in full in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7512` as an OSS bakery\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for bakers, pastry-cooks and\nconfectionery makers, following the SAME governed-actor architecture\nas every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Bakery\nCoordination Advisor ⊣ BakeryCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned\nidentically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different library\ncoordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **bakery scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct baking-execution or food-safety-clearance\nauthority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate\nexercising, or propose exercising a food-safety-clearance decision, an\nallergen-labeling determination, or any override of a shop safety\nofficer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind escalation --\nthey are structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- batch/inventory/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task/oven-schedule scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a burn-hazard/allergen-cross-\n  contamination/equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER\n  auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- baking-ingredients procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nfood-safety-clearance decision, an allergen-labeling determination, or\na shop-safety-officer-judgment override. These are **structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind\nescalation -- an op such as `:declare-batch-fit-for-sale` cannot even\nbe proposed by the reference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for`\nfunctions only ever emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any\ncode path (a forged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving\nfork) ever produced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD\ncheck (`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A\nsecond, independent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names six\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`bakerycoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:declare-batch-fit-for-sale`, `:finalize-food-safety-clearance`,\n`:finalize-batch-clearance-decision`,\n`:finalize-allergen-labeling-determination`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`bakerycoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-batch-fit-for-sale`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-food-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-allergen-labeling-determination`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Baker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered baker record (`:no-baker`). Never trusts\n   the proposal's own claim of who the baker is.\n2. **Bakery unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an independently\n   registered bakery site (`:no-bakery`). Together with check 1, this\n   directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a worker/bakery\n   record must be independently verified/registered before any\n   action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the six\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for declaring a batch fit for\n   sale, finalizing a food-safety-clearance decision, finalizing an\n   allergen-labeling determination, or overriding a shop safety\n   officer's judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks food-safety-clearance/allergen-labeling/\n   safety-override language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a burn-hazard/allergen-\n  cross-contamination/equipment-condition observation -- it never\n  resolves the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is\n  the hazard data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about shop\n  safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  baking-ingredients order is not itself unsafe, unlike a food-safety-\n  clearance or safety-officer-override attempt, which is why it is\n  handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural\n  absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"baking\", \"allergen\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside\nthe mock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate\nproposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly\nthe risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a bakery coordination actor\nworking adjacent to baking/allergen concerns necessarily discusses\nthose concepts to do its scheduling/logging job) could trigger if\nphrased carelessly. `bakerycoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is\nphrased exclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"declare\nthe batch fit for sale\", \"finalize the allergen-labeling\ndetermination\", \"override the shop safety officer's judgment\" --\nmatching the task's own worked example phrasing), never bare nouns,\nand\n`bakerycoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for baker ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\noven-shift task ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer review\")\nWITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action phrases, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-\nphrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this\nsession -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never\ntripped during development.\n`bakerycoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7512\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7512` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7512`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 21 tests, 45 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-batch-clearance` that is\n  merely gated behind an always-escalate list (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance --\n  an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  food-safety-clearance decision exists in the code path and is merely\n  deferred to a human gate. For a decision this severe (food safety,\n  allergen exposure), the capability itself must not exist. The only\n  op related to safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which\n  surfaces the need for human/shop-safety-officer attention and never\n  itself decides, clears, or defers a food-safety-clearance decision\n  for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold baking-\n  ingredients order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft\n  escalate gate, not a hard block; only the food-safety-clearance/\n  allergen-labeling/safety-officer-override class is a hard,\n  unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"baking\" \"allergen\"\n  \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase scope-\n  exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare nouns\n  -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses baking/allergen/\n  safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so a\n  bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale text that\n  deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Naming the excluded-op set after \"shop safety officer\" only, vs.\n  also naming a second distinct authority figure (mirroring house\n  building's dual safety-officer/foreman split): rejected -- the\n  task's domain design names only \"a shop safety officer's judgment\"\n  as the authority figure for this vertical, so a single\n  `:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment` op (plus a generic\n  `:override-safety-officer-judgment` alias and matching phrase\n  variants) fully covers the specified scope without inventing an\n  unspecified second authority role.\n- Merging `baker` and `bakery` into a single entity (only checking one\n  provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered baker AND independently-registered\n  bakery) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/bakery record\n  must be independently verified/registered before any action\" and\n  the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- batch/inventory/progress data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered baker AND bakery\n   (`:no-baker`/`:no-bakery`). Not a food-safety-clearance or\n   allergen-labeling decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task/oven-schedule\n   scheduling proposal only. Cannot carry a food-safety-clearance\n   decision (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such\n   attempt via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action`\n   content check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any\n   conclusion about a batch's safety -- it is a calendar/logistics\n   action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a burn-hazard/allergen-\n   cross-contamination/equipment-condition concern to a human/shop\n   safety officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every\n   confidence level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY\n   channel through which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it\n   explicitly never resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself --\n   the shop safety officer reviews and acts entirely on their own\n   authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- baking-ingredients procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not a food-safety-clearance or\n   authorization decision of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics\n   action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000\n   always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na food-safety-clearance decision (e.g. declaring a batch fit for\nsale), an allergen-labeling determination, or a shop-safety-officer-\njudgment override -- these categories are structurally absent, not\ngated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`bakerycoord.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) six concretely-named\nforbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit level\n(`bakerycoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`bakerycoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-batch-fit-for-sale`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-food-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-allergen-labeling-determination`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`bakerycoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to declare a batch fit for sale or override a shop\nsafety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`bakerycoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 21, :assertions 45, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Bakery Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :baker-verification :bakery-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7512", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7512", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7512], :test/simulator :bakerycoord.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7512 — Bakers, Pastry-cooks and Confectionery Makers Bakery Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7512}]